---

<DocShell
   title="MCP reference"
   summary="<p>The tools and resources of the a11ied MCP server. Each tool calls the same function as the CLI command it is named after, so results match.</p>"
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section>
      <h2 id="start">Start the server</h2>
      <pre><code>npx -y a11ied mcp</code></pre>
      <p>
         The server speaks MCP over standard input and output. It takes no options and opens
         no network port. Most clients start it from a configuration block:
      </p>
      <pre data-label="CONFIG"><code>{mcpConfig.trimEnd()}</code></pre>
      <p>
         See <a href="/guides/agents">use with an AI agent</a> for setup in specific agents.
         In a checkout of the repository, copy the entry in <code>mcp.example.json</code>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="tools">All tools</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
         <table>
            <thead>
               <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">CLI command</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>check</code></th><td>Scan a page and list what applies to it</td><td><code>a1 check</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>run_axe</code></th><td>Run axe-core</td><td><code>a1 axe</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>tree</code></th><td>Return the accessibility tree</td><td><code>a1 tree</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>capture</code></th><td>Screenshot a page in a chosen state</td><td><code>a1 capture</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>wcag_show</code></th><td>One criterion or technique</td><td><code>a1 wcag &lt;criterion&gt;</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>wcag_criteria</code></th><td>List or count criteria</td><td><code>a1 wcag criteria</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>wcag_rule</code></th><td>The criteria an axe rule tests</td><td><code>a1 wcag rule</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>search</code></th><td>Search criteria and patterns</td><td><code>a1 search</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>pattern_show</code>, <code>pattern_find</code></th><td>Look up ARIA patterns</td><td><code>a1 pattern</code>, <code>pattern role</code>, <code>pattern attribute</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>pattern_check</code>, <code>pattern_record</code>, <code>pattern_pending</code></th><td>Check a widget against a pattern</td><td><code>a1 pattern check</code>, <code>record</code>, <code>pending</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>sr_session</code></th><td>Start, open, stop, or inspect the session</td><td><code>a1 sr start</code>, <code>open</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>status</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>sr_action</code></th><td>One screen reader step</td><td>The other <code>a1 sr</code> commands</td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>sr_expect</code></th><td>Check an announcement</td><td><code>a1 sr expect</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>sr_transcript</code></th><td>Return or save the transcript</td><td><code>a1 sr transcript</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>sr_list</code></th><td>List named screen reader commands</td><td><code>a1 sr list</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>talkback</code></th><td>Drive TalkBack on Android</td><td><code>a1 talkback</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>audit_*</code></th><td>Run and report a WCAG audit</td><td><code>a1 audit</code></td></tr>
               <tr><th scope="row"><code>doctor</code></th><td>Report what is set up on the machine</td><td><code>a1 doctor</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
         </table>
      </div>
      <p>
         A few CLI commands have no tool. For <code>a1 sr walk</code>, call
         <code>sr_session</code> to start, <code>sr_action</code> with
         <code>read-all</code>, then <code>sr_transcript</code>. For <code>a1 sr batch</code>,
         call <code>sr_action</code> once per step. <code>a1 sr tail</code>,
         <code>a1 setup</code>, and <code>a1 audit dashboard</code> run until stopped or
         change the machine, so they stay in the terminal.
      </p>
      <p>
         Tools that take <code>version</code> default to WCAG <code>2.2</code>. The other value
         is <code>2.1</code>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="page">Page tools</h2>
      <p>
         <code>check</code>, <code>run_axe</code>, and <code>tree</code> take the page as
         <code>target</code>, a URL or file path, or as <code>html</code>, inline markup.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>check</code></dt>
         <dd><code>level</code>, <code>failOn</code>, <code>baseline</code>, <code>storageStatePath</code>, <code>timeoutMs</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>run_axe</code></dt>
         <dd>One of <code>level</code>, <code>criterion</code>, or <code>ruleIds</code> to choose rules. Also <code>selector</code>, <code>exclude</code>, <code>waitFor</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>viewport</code>, <code>headers</code>, <code>cookies</code>, <code>failOn</code>, <code>baseline</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>tree</code></dt>
         <dd><code>role</code> and <code>name</code> keep matching nodes and their ancestors. <code>click</code> opens a state first.</dd>
         <dt><code>capture</code></dt>
         <dd><code>url</code> and <code>out</code> are required. Also <code>viewport</code>, <code>zoom</code>, <code>textSpacing</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>press</code>, <code>hover</code>, <code>selector</code>, <code>fullPage</code>, <code>waitFor</code>, <code>storageStatePath</code>, <code>timeoutMs</code>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         <code>check</code> and <code>run_axe</code> return <code>verdict</code> and
         <code>exitCode</code>: 4 when a violation at or above <code>failOn</code> is not in
         <code>baseline</code>, otherwise 0. <code>baseline</code> is
         <code>&#123; acceptedFindings: [...] &#125;</code>, the content of a CLI baseline file.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="lookup">Lookup tools</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>wcag_show</code></dt>
         <dd><code>criterion</code>, required: a number such as <code>1.4.3</code>, a slug such as <code>contrast-minimum</code>, or a technique ID such as <code>G18</code>. Returns the criterion with its <code>testMethod</code> and <code>strategy</code>. <code>includeUnderstanding: true</code> adds the W3C's Understanding document.</dd>
         <dt><code>wcag_criteria</code></dt>
         <dd><code>level</code> narrows the list. <code>summary: true</code> returns counts by test method.</dd>
         <dt><code>wcag_rule</code></dt>
         <dd><code>ruleId</code>, required: an axe rule such as <code>color-contrast</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>search</code></dt>
         <dd><code>query</code>, required. <code>kind</code> keeps one kind of result. <code>limit</code> defaults to 10, with a maximum of 50.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>These read data that ships in the package. An agent can call them freely.</p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="pattern">Pattern tools</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>pattern_show</code></dt>
         <dd><code>name</code>: a pattern such as <code>combobox</code> or an example such as <code>combobox-select-only</code>. Leave it out to list every pattern.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern_find</code></dt>
         <dd>One of <code>role</code> or <code>attribute</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern_check</code></dt>
         <dd><code>pattern</code> and <code>selector</code>, required, plus <code>target</code> or <code>html</code>. <code>click</code> opens the widget first. <code>setup</code> and <code>table</code> reach a later state. Returns <code>exitCode</code> 4 for a documented key that did nothing or a missing attribute.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern_record</code></dt>
         <dd><code>pattern</code>, <code>row</code>, <code>selector</code>, and <code>outcome</code>, required. <code>outcome</code> is <code>passed</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>cantTell</code>, or <code>inapplicable</code>. Give the reason in <code>note</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>pattern_pending</code></dt>
         <dd><code>pattern</code> and <code>selector</code>, required. Returns the rows with no judgment yet.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="sr">Screen reader tools</h2>
      <h3>sr_session</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>action</code></dt>
         <dd>Required: <code>start</code>, <code>open</code>, <code>stop</code>, or <code>status</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>target</code></dt>
         <dd>On <code>start</code>: <code>voiceover</code>, <code>nvda</code>, or <code>virtual</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>allowVirtual</code></dt>
         <dd>On <code>start</code>: must be <code>true</code> to use <code>virtual</code> on a machine where VoiceOver or NVDA is the default. It makes the agent state that it accepts a simulation.</dd>
         <dt><code>url</code></dt>
         <dd>On <code>start</code> and <code>open</code>: the page to load.</dd>
         <dt><code>app</code>, <code>browser</code>, <code>recording</code>, <code>idleTimeoutMinutes</code>, <code>nativeInput</code></dt>
         <dd>On <code>start</code>: as the <a href="/reference/cli#sr"><code>a1 sr start</code></a> options.</dd>
         <dt><code>out</code>, <code>format</code>, <code>sessionId</code></dt>
         <dd>On <code>stop</code>: write the transcript, or retry a stop that failed.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         One session is active at a time, and <code>start</code> replaces it. The response's
         <code>session</code> has <code>target</code> and <code>targetType</code>:
         <code>real</code> or <code>simulated</code>. <code>status</code> returns
         <code>&#123; noSession: true &#125;</code> when there is none.
      </p>
      <h3>sr_action</h3>
      <p>
         Takes an <code>action</code> and, for some actions, a <code>payload</code>. These
         need no payload: <code>next</code>, <code>previous</code>, <code>top</code>,
         <code>bottom</code>, <code>activate</code>, <code>interact</code>,
         <code>stop-interacting</code>, <code>escape</code>, <code>read</code>,
         <code>title</code>, <code>transcript</code>. <code>next</code> and
         <code>previous</code> take <code>&#123; kind, level?, times? &#125;</code> to jump by
         heading, link, and so on.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>press</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; keys &#125;</code>, one chord per entry: <code>["Tab", "Tab"]</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>type</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; text &#125;</code></dd>
         <dt><code>goto</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; role?, name?, max? &#125;</code></dd>
         <dt><code>find</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; text &#125;</code></dd>
         <dt><code>elements</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; kind, max? &#125;</code></dd>
         <dt><code>read-all</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; max? &#125;</code></dd>
         <dt><code>table</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; move &#125;</code>, such as <code>next-cell</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>checkpoint</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; label &#125;</code></dd>
         <dt><code>wait</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; for?, since?, ms?, timeoutMs? &#125;</code></dd>
         <dt><code>perform</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; command, commandSet? &#125;</code>. Names come from <code>sr_list</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>focus</code></dt>
         <dd>One of <code>appName</code>, <code>bundleId</code>, <code>processName</code>, <code>pid</code>, <code>windowTitle</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>screenshot</code></dt>
         <dd><code>&#123; path &#125;</code>. VoiceOver only.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         Every response has <code>state</code>, with the announcement, the current element,
         and the transcript so far. A VoiceOver session adds <code>axFocusedElement</code>,
         the element that has keyboard focus. <code>goto</code>, <code>find</code>, and
         <code>wait</code> add <code>exitCode</code>: 4 when nothing matched.
      </p>
      <h3>sr_expect, sr_transcript, sr_list</h3>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>sr_expect</code></dt>
         <dd><code>pattern</code>, required: text, matched without regard to case, or <code>/regex/flags</code>. <code>since</code> limits it to what came after a checkpoint. <code>not</code> passes when nothing matches. Returns <code>exitCode</code> 4 and a <code>message</code> on failure.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr_transcript</code></dt>
         <dd><code>since</code>, <code>tail</code>, <code>afterIndex</code>, <code>limit</code>, and <code>out</code> to write a <code>.json</code> or <code>.md</code> file. <code>format</code> overrides the file type.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr_list</code></dt>
         <dd><code>query</code>, <code>sr</code>, <code>commandSet</code>. Pass <code>query</code>: the full list has several hundred entries.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="audit">Audit tools</h2>
      <p>
         These read and write the same audit as the <code>a1 audit</code> commands, so CLI
         and MCP workers can share one. Each takes an optional <code>audit</code> ID, except
         <code>audit_init</code> and <code>audit_list</code>. See
         <a href="/guides/audit">run an audit</a>.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs defs--wide">
         <dt><code>audit_init</code>, <code>audit_list</code></dt>
         <dd>Create an audit, or list the audits in the workspace.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_page</code></dt>
         <dd><code>action</code>: <code>add</code>, <code>list</code>, <code>exclude</code>, or <code>include</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_discover</code>, <code>audit_scan</code></dt>
         <dd>Add a site's pages, then run the automated checks on them.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_next</code></dt>
         <dd><code>worker</code>, required. Claims a unit and returns its work packet. <code>passes</code> and <code>excludePasses</code> choose the kind of work.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_submit</code></dt>
         <dd><code>worker</code>, <code>unit</code>, and <code>submission</code>, required. A rejection lists every problem.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_show</code>, <code>audit_note</code>, <code>audit_block</code>, <code>audit_reopen</code></dt>
         <dd>Inspect a unit, keep a claim alive, set a unit aside, or queue it again.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_limitation</code></dt>
         <dd>Record something the whole audit could not test.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_status</code>, <code>audit_signals</code></dt>
         <dd>Progress, and the scan's measurements for a page.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_findings</code>, <code>audit_finding</code></dt>
         <dd>List findings, and dismiss, merge, or rewrite one.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_report</code></dt>
         <dd>Write the report files.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="other">doctor and talkback</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>doctor</code></dt>
         <dd><code>task</code>: <code>all</code>, <code>scan</code>, <code>reader</code>, or <code>audit</code>. <code>target</code>: the screen reader to check. <code>recording: true</code> also checks screen recording.</dd>
         <dt><code>talkback</code></dt>
         <dd><code>action</code>, required: <code>on</code>, <code>off</code>, or <code>walk</code>. For <code>walk</code>, <code>key</code> and <code>count</code>. <code>serial</code> picks a device.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="resources">Resources</h2>
      <p>The server offers seven read-only resources, all JSON.</p>
      <dl class="defs defs--wide">
         <dt><code>a11ied://targets</code></dt>
         <dd>The screen readers a11ied supports.</dd>
         <dt><code>a11ied://wcag/criteria/2.2</code></dt>
         <dd>Every criterion.</dd>
         <dt><code>a11ied://wcag/levels/2.2</code></dt>
         <dd>The criteria at each level.</dd>
         <dt><code>a11ied://wcag/test-methods/2.2</code></dt>
         <dd>The test method and mapped rules for each criterion.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>The three WCAG resources also exist for <code>2.1</code>.</p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="effects">What each tool touches</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>Lookup tools, <code>pattern_show</code>, <code>pattern_find</code></dt>
         <dd>Read files in the package. Nothing else.</dd>
         <dt>Page tools, <code>pattern_check</code>, <code>audit_scan</code></dt>
         <dd>Open the page in a headless browser. <code>pattern_check</code> presses keys in it. <code>capture</code> writes an image file.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr_*</code> with <code>virtual</code></dt>
         <dd>Run a headless browser until the session stops.</dd>
         <dt><code>sr_*</code> with <code>voiceover</code> or <code>nvda</code></dt>
         <dd>Take control of the screen reader and a browser window on this machine, until <code>sr_session</code> is called with <code>stop</code>.</dd>
         <dt><code>audit_*</code>, <code>pattern_record</code></dt>
         <dd>Write to the <code>.a11ied</code> folder in the working directory.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>
</DocShell>
